1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,200
A company has a problem.

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:05,720
Somewhere among a thousand researchers,
one person can solve it.

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:07,153
Finding a name is easy.

4
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,140
Being right is not.

5
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:11,660
I am Asso, from SYSTASYS.

6
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:13,160
This is EINSTEIN Matchmaker.

7
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:18,920
Four agents read the same challenge at the
same time, on one model running on our own

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:19,760
machine.

9
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:21,020
No hosted API.

10
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:22,040
No key.

11
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:23,649
Nothing is sent to anyone.

12
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:26,460
Two of them think at the very same
instant.

13
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,294
You do not have to take my word for it.

14
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:33,540
The inference server records which of its
slots are busy, all the way through.

15
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:37,940
Five thousand of the nearly eight thousand
samples show two slots working at once.

16
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:40,020
Sixty three percent of the compute.

17
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:44,140
Then an independent critic reads the
proposal, and the sources under it.

18
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,220
Every claim has to quote a field, with its
record hash and a link into the
organizer's

19
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,480
own dataset. When the evidence is thin,
the system says no.

20
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:54,972
Out loud, with a reason.

21
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:59,040
In the verified block, two proposals were
accepted.

22
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:01,482
One was refused on the evidence.

23
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:03,000
Three ran out of time.

24
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:07,580
We count those three apart, because a case
that ends on the clock has said nothing
about

25
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:12,840
its sources. We do not claim that four
agents answer better than one.

26
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:18,280
There is no answer key for these
challenges, so that question stays open,
and the repository

27
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:19,960
says so in its first table.

28
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:24,360
A system that cannot refuse cannot be
trusted when it accepts.

29
00:01:24,440 --> 00:01:25,940
EINSTEIN Matchmaker.

30
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:30,785
The code, the traces and the verdicts are
all in the repository.
